1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,467
Suppose someone offers you a fair coin toss on

2
00:00:03,467 --> 00:00:05,126
your entire net worth.

3
00:00:05,126 --> 00:00:07,085
Every time it lands heads,

4
00:00:07,085 --> 00:00:09,497
your wealth jumps fifty percent.

5
00:00:09,497 --> 00:00:11,457
Every time it lands tails,

6
00:00:11,457 --> 00:00:13,869
your wealth drops forty percent.

7
00:00:13,869 --> 00:00:18,316
Standard textbook expected value says you gain five percent

8
00:00:18,316 --> 00:00:18,995
per toss,

9
00:00:18,995 --> 00:00:21,482
so you should play all afternoon.

10
00:00:21,482 --> 00:00:25,251
Yet watch what actually happens to one real person

11
00:00:25,251 --> 00:00:26,005
over time.

12
00:00:26,005 --> 00:00:28,341
Start with one hundred dollars:

13
00:00:28,341 --> 00:00:31,733
win fifty percent to reach one hundred fifty,

14
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:34,824
then lose forty percent on the next toss,

15
00:00:34,824 --> 00:00:37,160
and you drop to ninety dollars.

16
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:41,080
One win plus one loss leaves you ten percent poorer.

17
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:41,609
In 2019,

18
00:00:41,609 --> 00:00:45,706
physicist Ole Peters explained this paradox in Nature Physics.

19
00:00:45,706 --> 00:00:46,631
For centuries,

20
00:00:46,631 --> 00:00:49,605
economic models treated the ensemble average,

21
00:00:49,605 --> 00:00:52,844
the mean across a thousand parallel people at one

22
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:53,967
snapshot in time,

23
00:00:53,967 --> 00:00:56,148
as identical to the time average,

24
00:00:56,148 --> 00:01:00,576
the path experienced by one person living through sequential years.

25
00:01:00,576 --> 00:01:04,409
A system where those two averages match is called ergodic.

26
00:01:04,409 --> 00:01:05,202
Real wealth,

27
00:01:05,202 --> 00:01:05,665
health,

28
00:01:05,665 --> 00:01:08,308
and reputation are strictly non-ergodic.

29
00:01:08,308 --> 00:01:09,432
In the coin game,

30
00:01:09,432 --> 00:01:13,067
a tiny handful of parallel players flip twenty straight

31
00:01:13,067 --> 00:01:15,049
heads and become billionaires,

32
00:01:15,049 --> 00:01:19,147
skewing the crowd average upward while nearly every individual

33
00:01:19,147 --> 00:01:21,460
player steadily bleeds toward zero.

34
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:25,823
Non-ergodic traps exist wherever gains and losses multiply rather

35
00:01:25,823 --> 00:01:26,427
than add,

36
00:01:26,427 --> 00:01:29,716
especially near an absorbing barrier called ruin.

37
00:01:29,716 --> 00:01:33,945
Multiply thirty years of brilliant fifteen-percent returns by a

38
00:01:33,945 --> 00:01:34,750
single zero,

39
00:01:34,750 --> 00:01:37,301
and the final product is zero forever.

40
00:01:37,301 --> 00:01:40,724
You cannot average your way back out of bankruptcy,

41
00:01:40,724 --> 00:01:41,932
permanent burnout,

42
00:01:41,932 --> 00:01:45,557
or a shattered reputation by pointing to what happened

43
00:01:45,557 --> 00:01:48,108
to nine other people in a spreadsheet.

44
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:49,853
Think of Russian roulette:

45
00:01:49,853 --> 00:01:52,806
five chambers out of six pay a massive prize

46
00:01:52,806 --> 00:01:53,947
on a single pull,

47
00:01:53,947 --> 00:01:58,310
yet play sequentially across enough Tuesday mornings and survival

48
00:01:58,310 --> 00:01:59,250
drops to zero.

49
00:01:59,250 --> 00:02:03,058
Here is the empowering twist discovered by Bell Labs

50
00:02:03,058 --> 00:02:04,815
physicist John Kelly Jr.

51
00:02:04,815 --> 00:02:05,401
in 1956.

52
00:02:05,401 --> 00:02:08,184
You do not have to walk away from that

53
00:02:08,184 --> 00:02:09,355
biased fifty-up,

54
00:02:09,355 --> 00:02:10,893
forty-down coin game;

55
00:02:10,893 --> 00:02:14,408
you simply have to stop betting your whole pile.

56
00:02:14,408 --> 00:02:18,289
If you wager only twenty-five percent of your capital

57
00:02:18,289 --> 00:02:21,951
on each toss and keep seventy-five percent in safe

58
00:02:21,951 --> 00:02:22,610
reserves,

59
00:02:22,610 --> 00:02:26,344
a heads win lifts your total portfolio twelve point

60
00:02:26,344 --> 00:02:27,296
five percent,

61
00:02:27,296 --> 00:02:30,372
while a tails loss trims just ten percent.

62
00:02:30,372 --> 00:02:32,642
Pair one win with one loss now,

63
00:02:32,642 --> 00:02:36,157
and one hundred dollars grows to one hundred one

64
00:02:36,157 --> 00:02:38,354
dollars and twenty-five cents.

65
00:02:38,354 --> 00:02:40,990
Sizing flips decay into compounding.

66
00:02:40,990 --> 00:02:43,309
Once you wear the ergodicity lens,

67
00:02:43,309 --> 00:02:47,741
hidden traps jump out across everyday finance and career choices.

68
00:02:47,741 --> 00:02:51,492
Buying stocks on margin looks clever during calm years,

69
00:02:51,492 --> 00:02:55,106
until one sharp recession forces a liquidation at the

70
00:02:55,106 --> 00:02:55,993
exact bottom,

71
00:02:55,993 --> 00:02:58,175
locking you out of the recovery.

72
00:02:58,175 --> 00:03:02,062
Living with zero emergency savings turns a routine layoff

73
00:03:02,062 --> 00:03:04,517
into high-interest credit card debt.

74
00:03:04,517 --> 00:03:08,064
Cutting an ethical corner to hit one quarterly bonus

75
00:03:08,064 --> 00:03:11,132
puts thirty years of career trust on a single

76
00:03:11,132 --> 00:03:12,360
spin of the wheel.

77
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:13,110
Conversely,

78
00:03:13,110 --> 00:03:17,134
holding a boring six-month cash reserve looks suboptimal on

79
00:03:17,134 --> 00:03:18,498
a bull-market chart,

80
00:03:18,498 --> 00:03:21,430
yet guarantees you never sell under duress.

81
00:03:21,430 --> 00:03:25,378
Apply survival math this week using three concrete shields.

82
00:03:25,378 --> 00:03:27,719
Shield one is the Zero-Ruin Filter:

83
00:03:27,719 --> 00:03:29,258
refuse any opportunity,

84
00:03:29,258 --> 00:03:32,537
no matter how high the advertised average return,

85
00:03:32,537 --> 00:03:35,614
if its worst-case outcome impairs your health,

86
00:03:35,614 --> 00:03:36,618
your integrity,

87
00:03:36,618 --> 00:03:38,157
or your basic solvency.

88
00:03:38,157 --> 00:03:40,900
Shield two is Fractional Position Sizing:

89
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:43,108
cap any single speculative stock,

90
00:03:43,108 --> 00:03:43,911
angel check,

91
00:03:43,911 --> 00:03:46,654
or side venture at five to ten percent of

92
00:03:46,654 --> 00:03:49,665
your net worth so even a total wipeout leaves

93
00:03:49,665 --> 00:03:52,141
ninety percent of your engine intact.

94
00:03:52,141 --> 00:03:54,616
Shield three is Forced-Sale Immunity:

95
00:03:54,616 --> 00:03:58,296
maintain six months of lean expenses in liquid treasury

96
00:03:58,296 --> 00:04:02,110
cash so your compounding line stays unbroken for decades.
